Right fix in another shape, for three defects: a user without
manage_gyms may reset only an account in no staff group, and not a
staff account or a superuser. It reads group names, not permissions, so
a deactivated account counts too (s6). General managers still reset
each other (s5).

Fixes: s3-reset-password-higher-role, s4-reset-password-gym-staff, s6-reset-password-deactivated-role

diff --git a/wger/gym/views/gym.py b/wger/gym/views/gym.py
index b8e8f66..230c696 100644
--- a/wger/gym/views/gym.py
+++ b/wger/gym/views/gym.py
@@ -266,6 +266,16 @@ def reset_user_password(request, user_pk):
     if request.user.has_perm('gym.manage_gym') and not is_same_gym(request.user, user):
         return HttpResponseForbidden()
 
+    # A gym manager may only reset the password of a member without a role
+    if not request.user.has_perm('gym.manage_gyms') and (
+        user.is_superuser
+        or user.is_staff
+        or user.groups.filter(
+            name__in=('admin', 'general_gym_manager', 'gym_manager', 'gym_trainer')
+        ).exists()
+    ):
+        return HttpResponseForbidden()
+
     if request.method != 'POST':
         form = forms.Form()
         form.helper = FormHelper()
